To execute several actions and retry them if they fail:

```js
retryTo(() => {
  I.click('Link');
  I.see('Text')
}, 5)
```

Server component used to create an externally tracked ULT in following
code snippet:
{
    dss_create_ult(... , &thread);
    req = sched_req_get(attr, thread);
    if (req == NULL) {
        ABT_thread_free(thread);
        return error;
    }
}

The problem is that when sched_req_get() failed, there will be no way
to inform the 'thread' to abort, so the ABT_thread_free() on error
cleanup path would be blocked forever. (sched_get_req() usually won't
fail because most 'sched_request' are pre-allocated).

This patch introduced sched_create_ult() to solve above issue.

Signed-off-by: Niu Yawei <yawei.niu@intel.com>

This Pull Request adds some new features for the apisix charts, so that more and more APISIX features can be used.

1. Support to configure ETCD SNI;
2. Support to specify Plugin Attrs;
3. Support to use Pod UID as the APISIX instance id (see https://github.com/apache/apisix/issues/5417 for details).

Signed-off-by: Chao Zhang <tokers@apache.org>

Resolves #22673

